  "model_class": "cox_proportional_hazards",
  "rationale": "A cohort study design is appropriate to follow male infants over time and assess the risk of SUID. The Cox proportional hazards model allows for the inclusion of time-varying covariates (such as sleep environment if it were available) and can handle censored data, which is common in survival analysis.",
  "time_scale": {"source_id": "cdc", "name": "AGED"},
  "expected_direction": "The risk of SUID should be higher for male infants after reaching 44 weeks postconceptional age compared to before this age. The inclusion of sleep environment data would help determine if and how it modifies this risk pattern, but the current dataset does not capture this information, limiting our ability to draw definitive conclusions about its influence."
